# SFR-write manifest — regenerated by audit_sfr_writes.py --update.
# Every entry: ADDR  PATTERN  IMMEDIATE  # source-file(s)
# Any diff between the current .rst set and this file fails the
# audit gate. Update ONLY after reviewing what changed and
# confirming the new write is intentional.
#
# Bug precedent — 2026-07-22 flash #2 was `USBCTL = 0xC0`
# (assign,0xc0) at 0xfffc when Rev 20 has (or,0x80). A baseline
# generated from a working image would have flagged that
# specific tuple as a diff before flash.
#
# RE-BASELINED 2026-07-28, 68 -> 82 entries. The manifest had drifted
# several commits behind: --update had never been run since the endpoint
# and DMA work landed, so the gate was permanently red and therefore
# catching nothing. Each of the 14 added tuples traces to a completed,
# reviewed task, and all 14 are emitted by the HEAD build as well as the
# working tree (verified by diffing the emitted sets of both builds):
#
#   0xff68/0xffa8 (IEPCNF0/OEPCNF0) and_not 0xf7, or 0x08, or 0x20,
#     assign 0x84, runtime — EP0 STALL set/clear (bit 3) and data-toggle
#     (bit 5) from reply_stall() and the EP0 continuation path, plus the
#     UBME|DBUF configuration. Task #40 (SET_INTERFACE alt gating) and
#     the EP0 ordering fix.
#   0xffb2 (VECINT) runtime — the EP0 race fix: VECINT is now cleared
#     with a computed value at the TOP of each vector case, before the
#     next packet is armed (TI UsbEng.c engEx0, case IEP0_INT).
#   0xffd4 (CPTRXCNF4) assign 0x01, was 0x03 — hw_init.
#   0xffe2 (ACGDCTL) assign 0x10, was 0x00 — task #71, DMA arm writes.
#   0xfff6 (ACG2DCTL) runtime — same patch.
#   0xfffc (USBCTL) or 0x80 — see the annotated block below.
#   0xffff (USBFADR) assign 0x00 — address cleared on bus reset,
#     task #44 (VEC_RSTR handler).
#
# NOTE: the two writes this replaced (0xffd4 assign 0x03, 0xffe2 assign
# 0x00) are genuinely no longer emitted; they were superseded, not lost.

0xff2e  rmw       -       # usb
0xff60  assign    0x00    # streaming,usb
